        "--title",
        "comparison launch",
        "With GFM autolinking enabled, marked currently turns any text starting with \"www.\" into a link regardless of letter case, so \"Www.example.com\" and \"WWW.example.com\" become links. Per the GFM spec a bare www autolink must start with lowercase \"www.\" exactly; mixed- or upper-case variants must stay plain text. Scheme autolinks must remain case-insensitive for the scheme, so \"(See hTtPS://example.com/fhqwhgads.)\" must still produce a link with the trailing period excluded. Make \"www.\" detection case-sensitive without changing how http://, https:// or ftp:// are detected, and keep email autolinks working. Source lives under src/ (TypeScript); the library is built with npm run build:esbuild before tests run.\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npm run build:esbuild && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/."
